  "caption": "Split-half effects of averaging on decision stability.",
  "reading_guide": "Each pool connects the single-member reference on the left to the mean of ten members on the right; endpoints show stored means. The agreement axis is linear and the regret axis logarithmic. Values label the actual endpoints; short leader lines separate nearby labels without moving data. The 1,000 complementary 10/10 splits reuse the same 20 members, and each single-member reference averages all 100 cross-half pairs. Averaging lowers surrogate regret in all four pools; agreement in pools 11/12 remains 0.192/0.174. These are dependent split-half stability diagnostics, not independent replicates or an accuracy test of a future mean-of-twenty table.",
